        "original_id": "36212f9a-56b5-58f0-837e-f57fb86b1885",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jack Maitland, Alan Faneca, Darrelle Revis, Nick Mangold, Shaun Ellis, D’Brickashaw Ferguson\n- Organizations: National Football League, Pittsburgh Steelers, Seattle Seahawks, New York Jets\n- Products: Super Bowl ring, Vince Lombardi Trophy\n- Events: Super Bowl XL, 2010 Pro Bowl\n\nFacts:\n- Jack Maitland, born on February 8, 1948, is a former American football running back who played in the National Football League in the 1970s and earned a Super Bowl ring.\n- A Super Bowl ring is kept by players and team members as a collectible symbol of victory because only one Vince Lombardi Trophy is awarded to the winning team ownership.\n- Alan Faneca was selected six times as a first-team All-Pro and nine times for the Pro Bowl.\n- Alan Faneca won a Super Bowl ring with the Pittsburgh Steelers in Super Bowl XL when the Steelers defeated the Seattle Seahawks.\n- The New York Jets were represented at the 2010 Pro Bowl by Darrelle Revis, Nick Mangold, Shaun Ellis, D’Brickashaw Ferguson, and Alan Faneca.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "0336eafd-ecff-56ee-9a84-06bd1b3f6ec4",
        "text": "Page: Jack Maitland. Sentence: John Frederick \"Jack\" Maitland (born February 8, 1948) is a former American football running back in the National Football League in the 1970s and earned a Super Bowl ring.\nPage: Super Bowl ring. Sentence: Since only one Vince Lombardi Trophy is awarded to the team (ownership) itself, the Super Bowl ring offers a collectible memento for the actual players and team members to keep for themselves to symbolize the victory.\nPage: Alan Faneca. Sentence: A six-time first-team All-Pro and nine-time Pro Bowl selection, Faneca won a Super Bowl ring with the Steelers in Super Bowl XL, defeating the Seattle Seahawks.\nPage: 2009 New York Jets season. Sentence: The New York Jets were represented at the 2010 Pro Bowl by Darrelle Revis, Nick Mangold, Shaun Ellis, D’Brickashaw Ferguson, and Alan Faneca.",
